# Server-side only. Do NOT prefix with VITE_ — any VITE_-prefixed var is inlined
# into the browser bundle and would leak the key.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and paste a real key from Google AI Studio.
# Without a key set, /api/move falls back to a hardcoded legal move so the loop
# still runs end to end under `vercel dev`.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL — leave unset unless you're overriding. Global caps on ACTUAL Gemini calls
# (not /api/move requests — one request can make several calls via retries). These
# protect the project-wide free-tier quota from traffic spread across many IPs, which
# the per-IP limiter cannot see.
#
# The defaults live in api/move.js (`CALLS_PER_MIN` / `CALLS_PER_DAY`) and apply when
# these are unset — deliberately not repeated here, so this file can't drift out of
# date. Set them to match your real AI Studio limits, or to a low value to exercise the
# rate-limit path in the UI.
#
# Remember: .env.local is local-only. For production, set these in
# Vercel -> Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables.
#GEMINI_MAX_CALLS_PER_MIN=
#GEMINI_MAX_CALLS_PER_DAY=

# OPTIONAL — durable rate-limit store. Without these, the rate limiters fall back to an
# in-memory counter that resets on every request under `vercel dev` and on every cold
# start / per instance in production — i.e. it can't actually enforce a global cap.
# Point these at a Vercel KV or Upstash Redis instance (either var-name pair works) to
# make the limits genuinely shared and durable. Set them in the Vercel dashboard for
# production; pull to .env.local with `vercel env pull` for local testing.
#KV_REST_API_URL=
#KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
# (or, if using Upstash directly)
#UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
#UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
